## History:
##		- 20260318 JC: Created.
##		- 20260326 JC: Only `mount /boot/efi`, not `mount -a`.
##		- 20260327 JC: Fixed a logic error that was preventing proper mounting.
##		- 20260813 JC: Rewritten as a standalone script run by systemd.
##			- Was sourced into '/etc/rc.local' via '/etc/rc.localx9.d/020-insure-efi-mount', now retired to
##			  'legacy/'. Runs from 'tkz-insure-efi-mount.service', so the old 'sleep 5' is gone.
##			- No more 'sudo' per command while already root. Re-runs itself via sudo only for a normal user.
##			- Mountpoint is an argument, and the mount unit name comes from 'systemd-escape'.
##			- Prefers 'systemctl start <unit>.mount' over bare 'mount', and reports a masked mount unit,
##			  which was why this was needed at boot.
##			- Added '--check', '--dry-run' and '--wait', with real exit codes.
##			- Replaced the repeated flag blocks with small state functions.
